# The CRE's membership evaluation, and the cell it still refuses.
// ⭐ Rows 1–2 EVALUATE (T5b): newest-wins by date, then mechanical membership against the emitted set.
// ⚠ Row 3 is the cell that is still REFUSED — two candidates on the SAME DATE disagreeing, where the emitted
// `id` sort would decide and the CRE deliberately does not replicate it. It must refuse, never guess.
library "MembershipRefusalCases".
covers "MembershipRefusal".

fact "Pat":
- name is "Pat".
- birth date is "1970-01-01".
- defined by "Patient".

fact "RFA Request":
- code is "http://www.ama-assn.org/go/cpt|37718".
- date is "2026-01-01".
- defined by "ServiceRequest".

fact "Other Request":
- code is "http://www.ama-assn.org/go/cpt|37722".
- date is "2026-01-01".
- defined by "ServiceRequest".

// A clinician answers the SUBJECT — which service was requested — LATER than the request above.
fact "Answered Other":
- value is "http://www.ama-assn.org/go/cpt|37722".
- date is "2026-02-01".
- defined by "MembershipRefusal"."Requested Service".

case "covered service -> approve":
- subject is "Pat".
- fact is "RFA Request".
- result is "Membership Refusal Decision" is "Approve".

// ⭐ NEWEST WINS: an older covered request, overridden by a newer answer naming a non-covered service.
case "newer answer overrides an older covered request -> deny":
- subject is "Pat".
- fact is "RFA Request".
- fact is "Answered Other".
- result is "Membership Refusal Decision" is "Deny".

// ⚠ THE REFUSED CELL: same date, disagreeing codes. The tie-break is the emitted record id.
case "same-date disagreement -> refused":
- subject is "Pat".
- fact is "RFA Request".
- fact is "Other Request".
- result is "Membership Refusal Decision" is "Approve".
